      <data key="d1">content</data>
      <data key="d2">A phrase used by adolescents as a vague statement to avoid revealing true feelings.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-c5160492e097bac38980aeda-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-MENTALIZING-STANCE.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707412</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Avoiding Exploration Of True Feelings">
      <data key="d0">Avoiding Exploration Of True Feelings</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The act of steering away from examining or revealing one's genuine emotional state.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-c5160492e097bac38980aeda-chunk-000</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-MENTALIZING-STANCE.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707412</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Clear Curiosity">
      <data key="d0">Clear Curiosity</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A therapeutic technique that adopts a curious and unknowing stance, uses tentative language to express curiosity about an adolescent's inner state, and guides attention toward experience rather than factual filling.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-c5160492e097bac38980aeda-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-MENTALIZING-STANCE.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707412</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tentative Language">
      <data key="d0">Tentative Language</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Qualifying phrases such as "I'm not sure but...", "Maybe you...", "I guess you..." used to express uncertainty and invite correction or supplementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-c5160492e097bac38980aeda-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-MENTALIZING-STANCE.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707412</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Inner State">
      <data key="d0">Inner State</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The internal mental and emotional condition of an adolescent.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-c5160492e097bac38980aeda-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-MENTALIZING-STANCE.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707412</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Feeling Experience">
      <data key="d0">Feeling Experience</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The subjective quality of feelings and experiences explored jointly with the adolescent.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-c5160492e097bac38980aeda-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-MENTALIZING-STANCE.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707412</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Hypothesis">
      <data key="d0">Hypothesis</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A proposed statement or guess about the adolescent's inner state, put forward using tentative language to invite correction or supplementation.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-c5160492e097bac38980aeda-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-MENTALIZING-STANCE.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707412</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Automatic Mentalization Response under Normalized Pressure">
      <data key="d0">Automatic Mentalization Response under Normalized Pressure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The automatic mentalization response that occurs under normalized pressure, which the technique addresses.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Technique of Lowering Emotional Temperature through Empathy">
      <data key="d0">Technique of Lowering Emotional Temperature through Empathy</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A method that uses empathy to lower emotional temperature and promote mentalization recovery, involving steps of identifying signs, using empathic responses, and gently exploring inner states.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Emotional Temperature">
      <data key="d0">Emotional Temperature</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The level of emotional arousal or intensity that influences psychological intervention strategies; mentioned in the context of avoidance and keywords.&lt;SEP&gt;A metaphorical measure of emotional intensity; elevation indicates high arousal.&lt;SEP&gt;A concept representing the level of emotional arousal, which can be elevated and is lowered through empathy.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-000&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Mentalization Recovery">
      <data key="d0">Mentalization Recovery</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A process of restoring mentalization ability; associated with empathy and emotion regulation as keywords.&lt;SEP&gt;The restoration of the ability to mentalize, promoted by lowering emotional temperature.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Empathy">
      <data key="d0">Empathy</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A psychological concept listed as a keyword in the context of emotional support and mentalization recovery.&lt;SEP&gt;The capacity to understand and share feelings, used in the technique to lower emotional temperature.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001&lt;SEP&gt;doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-002</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Signs of Elevated Emotional Temperature">
      <data key="d0">Signs of Elevated Emotional Temperature</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Indicators such as agitation, silence, or conflict that signal an increase in emotional temperature.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Empathic Response">
      <data key="d0">Empathic Response</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A response that acknowledges and validates the adolescent's emotional experience, used to lower emotional temperature.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Gentle Exploration of Inner State">
      <data key="d0">Gentle Exploration of Inner State</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">A step that involves gently exploring the adolescent's inner mental state after emotional temperature has been lowered.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Normalized Pressure">
      <data key="d0">Normalized Pressure</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The condition of pressure that is considered normal, under which automatic mentalization responses occur.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Agitation">
      <data key="d0">Agitation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A state of restlessness or disturbance, mentioned as an example of a sign of elevated emotional temperature.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Silence">
      <data key="d0">Silence</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A state of being quiet or not speaking, mentioned as an example of a sign of elevated emotional temperature.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Conflict">
      <data key="d0">Conflict</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A disagreement or argument, mentioned as an example of a sign of elevated emotional temperature.</data>
      <data key="d3">doc-2526c2542d1fb9e5640b1a30-chunk-001</data>
      <data key="d4">GUIDANCE-TOPIC-AROUSAL.md</data>
      <data key="d5">1784707427</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
